\begin{abstract}
The increasing demand for efficient artificial intelligence has created a need for innovative solutions that balance model accuracy and computational resources. Existing approaches often compromise on one or the other, limiting their applicability in real-world scenarios. We introduce a novel framework that addresses this challenge by jointly optimizing model parameters and computational constraints, representing a significant departure from traditional methods. Our approach leverages a synergy between automated search and hardware-aware optimization, enabling the deployment of state-of-the-art models on resource-constrained devices. Experimental results demonstrate a substantial reduction in computational requirements while preserving model accuracy, with significant implications for on-device AI applications. The proposed framework achieves a notable improvement in efficiency, making it an attractive solution for a wide range of applications, and paving the way for further research in this area. By addressing the key challenges in efficient AI, our work enables the development of more powerful and efficient models, with potential applications in various fields.
\end{abstract}